Ionic gel electrolyte is a semi‑solid medium created by immobilizing a liquid electrolyte-typically a lithium salt dissolved in organic solvents or ionic liquids-within a polymer or inorganic gel matrix. This architecture delivers the high ionic conductivity of liquids while providing the mechanical stability, safety, and leak‑resistance characteristic of solid electrolytes.
