What is Ionic Gel Electrolyte?
Ionic gel electrolyte combines the best attributes of traditional liquid electrolytes and solid‑state materials. By entrapping the liquid phase in a three‑dimensional polymer network, the gel maintains high ionic mobility, enabling fast charge/discharge cycles, while preventing electrolyte leakage and enhancing thermal safety. The material can be engineered with a variety of polymer backbones-such as PVDF, PEO, PMMA, or emerging biopolymers-allowing manufacturers to tailor conductivity, elasticity, and temperature performance to specific battery architectures.
